WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.923
When keyword search beats embeddings, and when it doesn’t.

2
00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:08.152
Here is a working map, drawn from the sources above and from how the two methods are built.

3
00:00:08.432 --> 00:00:12.869
Treat it as a set of hypotheses to check on your own queries, not as rules.

4
00:00:13.149 --> 00:00:20.659
Keyword search tends to win on: Exact identifiers: error codes, SKUs, ticket numbers, clause numbers, version strings.

5
00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:28.256
Embeddings compress text into a few hundred or thousand dimensions, and nothing forces two different codes to land far apart.

6
00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:34.211
Names and rare terms: surnames, product names, internal project codenames, drug names.

7
00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:38.416
A rare term gets a high idf, which is exactly the right instinct.

8
00:00:38.696 --> 00:00:44.819
Vocabulary the embedding model never saw: new jargon, acronyms coined after its training data.

9
00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:47.765
BM25 needs no training at all.

10
00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:56.216
Explainability: you can show which terms matched and how much each contributed, which helps when a stakeholder asks why a result appeared.

11
00:00:56.496 --> 00:01:04.624
Embeddings tend to win on: Paraphrase and synonyms: “how do I get my money back” versus a document titled “Refund policy”.

12
00:01:04.904 --> 00:01:09.043
BM25 scores that pair at zero unless you add synonyms.

13
00:01:09.323 --> 00:01:13.205
Natural-language questions whose key words don’t appear in the answer.

14
00:01:13.485 --> 00:01:16.728
Cross-lingual search, with a multilingual embedding model.

15
00:01:17.008 --> 00:01:28.848
In a real team, the evidence to collect is a labeled set of queries tagged by type (identifier lookups, how-to questions, policy questions) and recall measured per type for each retriever.

16
00:01:29.128 --> 00:01:35.059
You’ll often find each method wins a different slice, which is the case for hybrid search in the next lesson.

17
00:01:35.339 --> 00:01:44.747
Anthropic’s experiments reached that conclusion across several knowledge domains: embeddings plus BM25 retrieved better than embeddings alone.
